    "title": "El Paso singer Julian Kalel's 'American Idol' journey ends",
    "text": "April 7, 2026, 11:21 a.m. MTFans are showing their love for El Paso singer Julian Kalel Almanzan whose journey on \"American Idol\" came to an end on Monday, April 6.Almanzan returned to season 24 of the singing competition this year after having to step down last year due to concerns with his mental health. This year, he came back stronger and with just as much support from judges Lionel Richie, Carrie Underwood and Luke Bryan.Last week, Almanzan made the Top 14 from votes from the previous O'hana week performances.On Monday, the show started with host Ryan Seacrest announcing the two performers who would be leaving, therefore leaving 12 contestants in the competition.On Tuesday, many fans of Almanzan were leaving encouraging words on his Instagram, telling him it's just the beginning.Almanzan said \"Thank you for your votes, your voices, your support, and for believing in me since the very beginning. (The) journey ain’t over yet, love every single one of y’all.\"After the contestants took the stage, one more singer was eliminated.Who went home on \"American Idol\" last night?Last week, host Ryan Seacrest didn't reveal a Top 12, leaving 14 contestants in the running. The episode started with those two eliminations.Almanzan, 19, was voted off. Jake Thistle, a 21-year-old from Paramus, New Jersey, was also eliminated.Both were gracious. Almanzan said, \"We appreciate being here. There are memories we will never forget.\"Then, the remaining 12 contestants performed '90s hits secretly chosen by the judges, Carrie Underwood, Lionel Richie and Luke Bryan. Jesse Findling, 19, from Massapequa Park, New York, was sent home at the end of last night's episode.Findling and Rae were in the bottom two after America voted. Richie, who won the judges' song contest, got to save one of them. He chose Rae, sending Findling back to New York.María Cortés González may be reached at 915-546-6150; mcortes@elpasotimes.com; @eptmaria.bsky.social on Bluesky, and @eptmariacg on TikTok.",
